            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kel Habicht-Berg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "so i really had to doctor this but it did turn out well. i used only 1 clove of garlic. i followed the recipe on everything else and then when i tasted it i really thought the vinegar was too strong. i added a few more tablespoons of oil and a few quick dashes of water. i made it to put over a salmon salad. also if you are making this for more than one person and you like a lot of dressing you may want to double the recipe. i also like that you don't have to worry about the dressing separating as it sits well because of the heaviness of the dijon.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-20T00:38:47.380Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
